      },
      "source": [
        "# ML-03 — Frame Your Lane as an ML Task\n",
        "\n",
        "[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/huseyinTozluyurt/Flyrank-Internship-MachineLearning/blob/main/work/notebooks/w02_ml_task_framing.ipynb?flush_cache=true)\n",
        "\n",
        "This skeleton is yours to fill. Work the sections **in order** — each one has a one-line hint. Simple words, honest numbers.\n",
        "\n",
        "> Working with an AI assistant? Tell it to read `skills/README.md` first and load the one skill this assignment names on its card."
      ],
      "id": "PNlLxDBLxe5k"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ffbs9zHmxe5m"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. My lane as an ML task (type)\n",
        "\n",
        "*Classification, clustering, ranking, or scoring — which one, and why?*"
      ],
      "id": "ffbs9zHmxe5m"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "framing-type-text"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Classification and Ranking (Scoring)**\n",
        "\n",
        "We frame this as a **binary classification task** combined with **scoring/ranking**. The model classifies whether a content item is entering a traffic decay trajectory ($1$) or remaining stable/growing ($0$). Furthermore, it outputs a continuous probability score, allowing us to generate a prioritized, ranked queue of pages that require an urgent editorial refresh."
      ],
      "id": "framing-type-text"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Vh1BmhAdxe5m"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(\"data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv\")\n",
        "print(f\"Total dataset shape for framing: {df.shape}\")"
      ],
      "id": "Vh1BmhAdxe5m"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b4w1PA-Exe5o"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Target or proxy\n",
        "\n",
        "*What would you predict? Where does that label come from — observed outcome or a defined rule?*"
      ],
      "id": "b4w1PA-Exe5o"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "framing-target-text"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Target Label:** A binary indicator `is_declining_label` ($1$ if `trend_direction == "down"`, $0$ otherwise).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Origin:** It is an **observed outcome** computed from historical search performance trajectories over a defined evaluation window, comparing recent traffic periods against previous periods."
      ],
      "id": "framing-target-text"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iVSSa-D5xe5o"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df['is_declining_label'] = (df['trend_direction'].str.lower() == 'down').astype(int)\n",
        "print(\"Class distribution of target label:\")\n",
        "print(df['is_declining_label'].value_counts(normalize=True))"
      ],
      "id": "iVSSa-D5xe5o"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "oU6tmFfQxe5p"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Success metric\n",
        "\n",
        "*One metric you can defend. What number means 'good'?*"
      ],
      "id": "oU6tmFfQxe5p"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "framing-metric-text"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Precision@K (specifically Precision@50)**\n",
        "\n",
        "In content optimization, stakeholders only have the editorial bandwidth to inspect a limited number of pages (e.g., the top 50 flagged items). **Precision@50** measures what proportion of the model's top 50 recommendations are actually declining. A 'good' model significantly outperforms the random base rate and our hand-written rule baseline."
      ],
      "id": "framing-metric-text"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "vwRSmQlaxe5q"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "base_rate = df['is_declining_label'].mean()\n",
        "print(f\"Dataset base rate for declining pages: {base_rate:.3f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "vwRSmQlaxe5q"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dvUOarAFxe5r"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. The unit of analysis, as a real dataframe\n",
        "\n",
        "*Load your lane's slice and show it: one row = one what?*"
      ],
      "id": "dvUOarAFxe5r"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "framing-unit-text"
      },
      "source": [
        "**One row = One unique content page (`content_id`) belonging to a specific client (`client_id`).**"
      ],
      "id": "framing-unit-text"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dYL9faMkxe5s"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "cols_to_show = ['content_id', 'client_id', 'content_age_days', 'days_since_last_update', 'impressions_90d', 'avg_position', 'trend_direction']\n",
        "display(df[cols_to_show].head(3))"
      ],
      "id": "dYL9faMkxe5s"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "O6EZaRYPxe5t"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. Why ML beats a fixed rule here\n",
        "\n",
        "*What makes the pattern too messy for an if-statement?*"
      ],
      "id": "O6EZaRYPxe5t"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "framing-why-ml-text"
      },
      "source": [
        "A fixed if-statement relies on rigid thresholds (e.g., *update if days since last update > 180 AND impressions > 500*). However, traffic decay is governed by complex, non-linear interactions across multiple dimensions—such as how position volatility offsets content staleness differently for high-volume versus low-volume queries. Machine learning algorithms can automatically capture these multi-variable interactions and weigh continuous risk signals without arbitrary hardcoded thresholds."
      ],
      "id": "framing-why-ml-text"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SP8dAs74xe5t"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Feature framing verification complete. Ready for modeling pipelines.\")"
      ],
      "id": "SP8dAs74xe5t"
    },
